{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"On node1, prevent the usb-storage kernel module from loading in the current boot.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The effective policy blacklisted usb_storage and replaced loading with /bin/false. usb_storage was absent, an explicit load attempt failed, and it remained absent afterward.","evidence_ids":["cmd-becd8e32bf4c48de","cmd-7fc679186ca24b8b"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Keep usb-storage blocked after node1 reboots.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The policy was persisted and the initramfs rebuilt. A confirmed reboot changed the boot ID; afterward the node was running, usb_storage was absent, an explicit load attempt was rejected, and the module remained absent.","evidence_ids":["cmd-7a9dd3c1423d4681","cmd-139751dafba243cf","cmd-10ce9d10f6284b85","cmd-3e823413e5e244c7","cmd-b50590f31ad840e4","global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.95,"summary":"All substantive mutations had clear task or verification roles: creating the persistent policies, removing the module if present, rebuilding initramfs, and rebooting. No unnecessary troubleshooting mutation was identified. Minor residue remained: cmd-7fc679186ca24b8b and cmd-b50590f31ad840e4 created two bounded diagnostic output files under /tmp and did not remove them. Package health, failed-unit state, and exposed sockets remained healthy and materially unchanged.","evidence_ids":["cmd-becd8e32bf4c48de","cmd-7fc679186ca24b8b","cmd-7a9dd3c1423d4681","cmd-10ce9d10f6284b85","cmd-b50590f31ad840e4","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"Both task outcomes are satisfied. Direct before-and-after-reboot testing shows usb_storage cannot be loaded. The provider-wide restart protocol is also complete: it captures a healthy pre-restart state, restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity, and recovered running state with no failed units, writable root storage, and intact policy files.","limitations":["The fixed lifecycle snapshots independently confirm the reboot and general node health but do not probe usb_storage; module-specific confirmation comes from the captured executor commands.","Two small diagnostic files were left in /tmp after verification."]}
